        "id": 118978,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-11T01:06:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Whether we're only doing one \"chain\" or everyone starts their own and \"passes it to the next person\" (like in Droodles), how many times do we go around before we stop? It's not like we're using paper that'll run out of space ;).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>For each chain, everyone has one turn, so if we have 8 players there will be 4 pictures and five sentences, assuming I give the starting sentences. You don't want people to contribute again to a single chain because they'll likely remember the original information they had and that will mess things up.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:52:02.510Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
